
---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cardio Workouts | Silken Valley Lifestyle"
  description="Explore walking, jogging, running, cycling, indoor cardio, and interval training for cardiovascular fitness."
  heroTitle="Cardio Workouts"
  heroText="Energizing activities to build endurance, improve stamina, and support an active lifestyle."
  heroCompact={true}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Fitness & Active Living</p>
    <h1>Cardiovascular Fitness & Endurance</h1>
    <p>
      Cardiovascular exercise is an important part of a balanced
      fitness routine. Whether you enjoy walking outdoors,
      cycling through scenic surroundings, or exercising at home,
      discover enjoyable ways to improve endurance and make
      regular movement part of everyday life.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cardio-intro">
    <h2>The Benefits of Cardio Exercise</h2>
    <p>
      Regular aerobic activity supports heart and lung health,
      builds stamina, improves circulation, and contributes
      to overall physical wellbeing. Choose activities that
      suit your interests and current fitness level, and
      gradually increase duration and intensity as your
      endurance develops.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cardio-grid">
    <article class="cardio-card">
      <span class="cardio-number">01</span>
      <h2>Walking for Fitness</h2>
      <p>
        Walking is an accessible way to build an active lifestyle.
        Enjoy a brisk walk outdoors, explore local trails, or
        incorporate short walking sessions into your daily routine.
      </p>
      <h3>Getting Started</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Begin with a comfortable 15–20 minute walk.</li>
        <li>Gradually increase your walking time.</li>
        <li>Experiment with gentle hills and varied terrain.</li>
        <li>Choose supportive walking shoes.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="cardio-card">
      <span class="cardio-number">02</span>
      <h2>Jogging & Running</h2>
      <p>
        Jogging and running are effective aerobic activities
        that can improve cardiovascular endurance and stamina.
        A gradual walk-and-jog approach can help beginners
        develop confidence.
      </p>
      <h3>Getting Started</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Begin with a five-minute walking warm-up.</li>
        <li>Alternate short jogging intervals with walking.</li>
        <li>Increase running time gradually.</li>
        <li>Allow adequate recovery between sessions.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="cardio-card">
      <span class="cardio-number">03</span>
      <h2>Cycling</h2>
      <p>
        Cycling offers an enjoyable aerobic workout, whether
        outdoors on local roads and trails or indoors on a
        stationary bicycle. It is also a relatively low-impact
        way to build endurance.
      </p>
      <h3>Getting Started</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Start with 15–20 minutes at an easy pace.</li>
        <li>Adjust resistance to suit your fitness level.</li>
        <li>Maintain a comfortable cycling position.</li>
        <li>Increase duration as your stamina improves.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="cardio-card">
      <span class="cardio-number">04</span>
      <h2>Indoor Cardio</h2>
      <p>
        Indoor cardio makes it easy to stay active regardless
        of the weather. Try a stationary bike, treadmill,
        elliptical machine, or simple movement routines
        at home.
      </p>
      <h3>Ideas to Try</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Marching in place.</li>
        <li>Step-ups on a suitable stable step.</li>
        <li>Stationary cycling.</li>
        <li>Beginner aerobic movement routines.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="cardio-card">
      <span class="cardio-number">05</span>
      <h2>Interval Training</h2>
      <p>
        Interval training alternates periods of increased
        activity with easier recovery periods. It can be
        adapted to walking, cycling, jogging, and many
        other forms of aerobic exercise.
      </p>
      <h3>A Simple Example</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Warm up with five minutes of easy movement.</li>
        <li>Walk briskly for one minute.</li>
        <li>Walk comfortably for two minutes.</li>
        <li>Repeat several times at a manageable pace.</li>
        <li>Finish with a gentle cool-down.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="cardio-card">
      <span class="cardio-number">06</span>
      <h2>Outdoor Activities</h2>
      <p>
        Make cardiovascular exercise enjoyable by incorporating
        outdoor activities into your week. Fresh air, changing
        scenery, and time outdoors can make regular movement
        feel less like a chore.
      </p>
      <h3>Activities to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Hiking and nature walks.</li>
        <li>Swimming.</li>
        <li>Recreational cycling.</li>
        <li>Cross-country skiing and seasonal activities.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="cardio-routine">
    <p class="eyebrow">Planning & Consistency</p>
    <h2>Creating a Weekly Cardio Routine</h2>
    <p>
      A consistent routine can help make cardiovascular
      exercise a lasting habit. The following is an example
      of a balanced week that can be adjusted to individual
      fitness levels, schedules, and recovery needs.
    </p>

    <div class="routine-table">
      <div class="routine-row">
        <strong>Monday</strong>
        <span>Brisk walking – 20 to 30 minutes</span>
      </div>
      <div class="routine-row">
        <strong>Tuesday</strong>
        <span>Easy cycling – 20 minutes</span>
      </div>
      <div class="routine-row">
        <strong>Wednesday</strong>
        <span>Rest or gentle movement</span>
      </div>
      <div class="routine-row">
        <strong>Thursday</strong>
        <span>Walk-and-jog intervals – 20 minutes</span>
      </div>
      <div class="routine-row">
        <strong>Friday</strong>
        <span>Indoor cardio – 20 minutes</span>
      </div>
      <div class="routine-row">
        <strong>Saturday</strong>
        <span>Outdoor walk or recreational activity</span>
      </div>
      <div class="routine-row">
        <strong>Sunday</strong>
        <span>Rest and recovery</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cardio-note">
    <h2>Exercise at Your Own Pace</h2>
    <p>
      If you are new to exercise, begin with shorter sessions
      and comfortable intensity. Build up gradually, include
      recovery days, and pay attention to how your body feels.
      Stop if you experience chest pain, dizziness, or unusual
      shortness of breath, and seek appropriate medical advice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cardio-links">
    <h2>Explore More Workouts</h2>
    <div class="cardio-link-grid">
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/strength-training/">Strength Training →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/home/">Home Workouts →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/low-impact/">Low-Impact Exercise →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="cardio-back">
    <a href="/fitness/workouts/">← Return to Workouts</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .cardio-intro {
    margin: 30px 0;
    padding: 28px;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .cardio-intro h2,
  .cardio-routine h2,
  .cardio-note h2,
  .cardio-links h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .cardio-intro p,
  .cardio-routine > p:not(.eyebrow),
  .cardio-note p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cardio-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 35px 0;
  }

  .cardio-card {
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .cardio-number {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .cardio-card h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 13px;
  }

  .cardio-card h3 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
  }

  .cardio-card p,
  .cardio-card li {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .cardio-card p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cardio-card ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .cardio-routine {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .cardio-routine .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .routine-table {
    margin-top: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .routine-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr;
    gap: 15px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .routine-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .routine-row strong {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
  }

  .routine-row span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .cardio-note {
    padding: 30px;
    margin: 40px 0;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .cardio-links {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .cardio-link-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 15px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .cardio-link-grid a {
    display: block;
    padding: 18px;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .cardio-link-grid a:hover {
    background: var(--rose-wash);
  }

  .cardio-back {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .cardio-back a {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .cardio-back a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .cardio-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .cardio-link-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .routine-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 5px;
    }
  }
</style>
